只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Bridge the Pi and DeepSeek Harness ecosystems: one Pi Host ABI runs unmodified Pi extensions as native DSH plugins. 打通 Pi 与 DSH 生态。","id":"gh:1333452358","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"pi2dsh","slug":"weijiafu14/pi2dsh","topics":["ai-agents","compatibility-layer","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","migration","pi","pi-agent","plugin-migration"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Bridge the Pi and DeepSeek Harness ecosystems: one Pi Host ABI runs unmodified Pi extensions as nati"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ve DSH plugins. 打通 Pi 与 DSH 生态。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# pi2dsh"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**Move a Pi setup to DeepSeek Harness without rebuilding it.** The\nextensions, MCP manager, subagent"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"s, memory and background tasks you use on Pi\ninstall on DSH as the same npm packages and run unmodif"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ied — web, terminal\nand headless."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"MCP is the deepest-verified path: the full protocol surface — OAuth,\nresources, prompts, MCP Apps, e"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"licitation, sampling, cancellation — runs\nthrough DSH's own approval and rendering\n(evidence matrix)"},{"id":"p6s3","text":". What has been verified end to\nend is listed in What actually works today;\nnothing outside that tab"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"n verified end to\nend is listed in What actually works today;\nnothing outside that table is claimed."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Version support is explicit:"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| pi2dsh | DSH host | Maintenance |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"| 0.28.0-next.1 (`next`) | 0.2.2-alpha.3 | Pi 1.4 preview: acceptance and limits |\n| 0.27.1 | 0.2.1-"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"rc.2 / 0.2.1-rc.3 | Acceptance and release status |\n| 0.27.0 | 0.2.1-rc.2 | Acceptance and release s"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"tatus |\n| 0.26.0 | 0.2.0-rc.2 | Release verification |\n| 0.25.2 | 0.1.5-rc.2 | Frozen checkpoint: re"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" | 0.2.0-rc.2 | Release verification |\n| 0.25.2 | 0.1.5-rc.2 | Frozen checkpoint: release evidence |"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Published 0.27.x uses Pi 0.84.1; the 0.28 candidate targets Pi 1.4.0 with explicitly\ndocumented capa"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"bility limits. New engine releases target the\nvalidated current DSH line; historical fixes start fro"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"m their release tag when\nneeded. DSH owns stored-session format migration. An untested host version "},{"id":"p10s4","text":"is\nnot included in the compatibility declaration."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"For the **0.27.x / DSH 0.2.1** line, the validated terminal packages are\n`@deepseek-harness-tui/dsh-"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"tui@0.17.0` and `@xmoon76/dsh-pi-tui@0.5.3`.\nThe older dsh-pi-tui 0.5.1 still references removed hos"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"t components; upgrade\nthat terminal rather than bypassing compatibility checks with `allow-version`."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"For DSH 0.2.2-alpha.3, use `pi2dsh@next` (or Web suite `dsh-work-x@next`)\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Why this exists"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness is built\non ideas worth betting on — a durable, reconstructable session log, a clea"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"n\nservice composition, an agent loop you can actually reason about. Its plugin\necosystem is young. P"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"i has a mature one: hundreds of\npublished packages, many with real users."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"pi2dsh is one compatibility layer that implements Pi's public extension ABI on\ntop of DSH's native s"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"ervices, so a Pi package runs on DSH **as published** —\nno fork, no patch, no per-package adapter. F"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"or a Pi user or team that means\nswitching hosts without rebuilding the toolchain; for a Pi plugin au"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"thor it\nmeans a second host with no port to maintain. To the user everything looks\nlike DSH; to the "},{"id":"p15s5","text":"plugin everything looks like Pi."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"At the same time, pi2dsh is an ongoing, full-surface, real-world test of DSH's\narchitecture. Instead"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" of patching individual plugins, it asks whether the\nmodels, tools, sessions, interaction, resources"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" and client capabilities that Pi\nplugins rely on can preserve their logic and lifecycle using only D"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"SH's public\nservices and extension seams. If they can, that is strong evidence that DSH's\narchitectu"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"ral goals for building agents and an agent-plugin ecosystem have been\nachieved, at least along this "},{"id":"p16s6","text":"dimension. Wherever the bridge must bypass,\ndegrade or cannot express a capability, it pinpoints an "},{"id":"p16s7","text":"architectural gap that\nremains."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## What actually works today"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Two levels, and they are not the same claim."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Three layers, and nothing crosses them:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"DSH is two halves, and so is the bridge. The column above is the server; the\nbrowser shell has its o"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"wn plugin surface, and a Pi capability that is a SHAPE\nrather than a behaviour lands there:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"The browser half's data rides **this package's own route**, not DSH's typed\nRemote system: that one "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"is a first-party, code-generated contract, and an\nout-of-tree plugin talking to its own UI should ca"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"rry its own channel. One\npayload per session serves every seat — the side-conversation panel, plus t"},{"id":"p24s4","text":"he\nPi presentation surfaces (status, widget, header, footer, title and the\nworking/thinking chrome),"},{"id":"p24s5","text":" which are drawn in the host's own slot seats rather\nthan re-implemented. Two host rules make the br"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"owser half load at all — the\npackage must export `./package.json` (the host resolves the manifest by"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"\nsubpath), and the `./client` bundle is a closure-factory artifact, not plain\nESM."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"The rules that keep it honest:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- **Never a second bridge-owned implementation of something DSH already has.**\nTools go to DSH's too"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"l registry, models to DSH's llm configuration,\nconfiguration-only MCP servers to `dsh-mcp-client`, s"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"kills to\n`dsh-skill-filesystem`, and questions to DSH's user questions. An explicitly\ninstalled Pi c"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"apability package can retain behavior that it owns; the bridge\nmaps its public surfaces and does not"},{"id":"p26s5","text":" copy its transport.\n- **No bridge-private user world.** Normal configuration remains DSH-shaped:\nDS"},{"id":"p26s6","text":"H settings, commands and credentials. When an installed capability package\ndeliberately exposes its "},{"id":"p26s7","text":"own manager, that surface remains recognizable and\nis namespaced on conflict — dsh-TUI keeps `/mcp`,"},{"id":"p26s8","text":" while the Pi manager is\n`/pi-mcp`.\n- **No per-package special cases.** The core contains no\n`if (pa"},{"id":"p26s9","text":"ckageName === …)`. One ABI gap fixed unlocks every package that hits\nit.\n- **Never fake success.** A"},{"id":"p26s10","text":" capability with no safe mapping is reported —\nonce, per plugin, in plain language — instead of sile"},{"id":"p26s11","text":"ntly returning\nsomething invented. If a plugin needs one during startup, it is marked\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## What this is teaching us about DSH"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"pi2dsh is also an executable stress test of DSH's plugin architecture. Pi gives\nthat test a useful w"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"orkload: a large, already-used public plugin ABI rather than\na set of examples invented to fit the h"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"oad: a large, already-used public plugin ABI rather than\na set of examples invented to fit the host."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The result so far is specific, not a thumbs-up/thumbs-down verdict:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"- DSH's public seams successfully carry whole capabilities: tools, commands,\nmodel adapters, user qu"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"estions, native child sessions and browser slots.\n- The pressure points appear when an out-of-repo p"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"lugin needs to extend an\nexisting capability *from the inside*: add a durable session-event type,\nin"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"tercept the real provider request/response, control compaction before it\nhappens, or participate in "},{"id":"p30s5","text":"trust before project resources load.\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
